    35	Berlekamp’s algorithm in 1970 [Ber70]. Since then, there has been a significant amount of
    36	work on algorithms for this central problem (see surveys [vzGP01], [Kal03], [vzG06]). A key
    37	development due to Kaltofen and Shoup in 1998 [KS98] was the first sub-quadratic algorithm
    38	for this problem. The current best exponent is3/2, achieved by Kedlaya and Umans [KU11]
    39	via a new nearly-linear-time algorithm for modular composition.
    40	These asymptotically fastest algorithms use the framework pioneered by Cantor and
