     9	from 1 through n. Umans and Wang proposed, as the arithmetic-progression version of
    10	their Strong ( α, β)-Divisor Conjecture, an n-divisor arithmetic progression having at most
    11	n2β terms, each of magnitude at most exp(nα). We prove unconditionally that an n-divisor
    12	arithmetic progression of heightHwith logH=o( √n) must have length
