UW’s proof does use only prime coverage and explicitly recovers multiplicities by trial division. Two qualifications matter: nonzero witnesses must be enforced, and the proposed mass constraint bounds how many target primes one difference can carry; it does not force every witness to be smooth. I’m checking how much of He–Sahai’s incidence argument survives in higher rank.
