codex
I have a conditional rank-two extension: He–Sahai’s bound survives when no nonzero difference is divisible by two band primes and the shorter side is sufficiently small. This leaves balanced rank-two GAPs open. The literature also separates growing strings of smooth numbers from the requested scale: Balog–Wooley’s results do not provide prime coverage or fast factorizations of every cross-difference.
